WEBVTT

00:01:48.030 --> 00:01:50.450
Is Rikako eating properly?

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:54.920
I wonder... she has locked herself up
in the engine room all this while.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.600
Once she starts on something, she forgets
night and day, exactly like somebody I know.

00:02:00.910 --> 00:02:02.710
Aren't you really looking forward to it?

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:05.050
Not really.

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:11.040
But perhaps just a little, since she herself said she wanted to do it.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.180
<i>Metropolitan Expressway at midnight</i>

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:16.970
That man who drives the Lan Evo with a Naniwa number.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:17.870
Eiji-san?
<i>Metropolitan Expressway at midnight</i>

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:18.310
Eiji-san?

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:22.310
I heard he's helping out at RGO.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:28.060
He found a good job, since he can drive
around and remember the roads here.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.070
I heard that this Eiji is going after the Z.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.410
Since it's that kind of car, that Z...

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:38.390
Ok, let's go. Bring it up to 5th gear.

00:02:46.510 --> 00:02:49.620
Yama-san, delivery is due tomorrow for this, right?

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:50.960
Yeah.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.480
Can you check the setting one more time?

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:58.190
The top end of the 5th gear looks pretty dangerous.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:00.610
How's the air filter system?

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.520
It's not bad, but...

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:05.690
I got it, I'll recheck.

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:10.130
Hey, hey, isn't this the engine that was made really carefully?

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:15.090
Yes, but if Eiji is worried, I'll check it again.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.170
Well, that's fine.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:22.210
Sorry, I'm rather particular with things.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:25.410
If there's something bothering me, I can't drive it.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:29.330
You're really are an oil-type person.

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.110
There's a saying from long ago about two types of car lovers.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:39.140
Those with gasoline circulating in their
bloodstream, and those with oil circulating instead.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:42.070
In other words, the driving-types and modifying-types.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.770
You're a modifying-type.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.480
Oh! A rare guest.

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.940
Why are you together with BlackBird?

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:11.320
For various reasons... by the way, how is the Lan Evo?

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:12.950
You guys are re-modifying it, right?

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.720
You're well informed. We're in the middle of it now.

00:04:18.220 --> 00:04:19.210
Yo.

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.940
It's been a while and I feel like riding next to you.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.820
You changed Tominaga's setting by yourself again.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.100
Seems like you noticed immediately.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.900
But it didn't improve at all.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.950
No, it's not bad, it fits your style.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:51.490
An R. It looks fast. Aren't you going to chase it?

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.330
It's alright. It feels different.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.490
You can tell, right?

00:04:56.110 --> 00:05:02.350
I can now feel whether it's the same or
different, at the moment I see it, without fail.

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:05.880
I only want to race with people I can connect with.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.880
Does Eiji have it?

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:13.550
He does. I felt it clearly when I met
him at the Shutokou the other day.

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:22.270
Actually, we made a simulation of the Z, BlackBird
and Eiji's Lan Evo on Tominaga's computer.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:28.980
If we rate BlackBird as 10, the Lan Evo can
go up up 12 depending on the tuning.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.880
But Z's limit is at 8, no matter the setting.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.030
That means it has power, but it's not efficient.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:39.500
Though we've already known that all along.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:43.510
I think Tominaga-san's simulation is quite accurate.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:48.260
However, you and Tominaga-san know very well, too.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:52.980
That there's something about this Z
which can never be logically figured out...

00:05:54.130 --> 00:06:00.600
But I know one way to make the limit go from 8 to 9.

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:07.480
The fuel system will remain an analog carburetor
but we get power from the CPU for ignition.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:10.500
You mean control the ignition system with the CPU?

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:15.000
No, not the system itself, but the timing of he ignition.

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:18.590
The Z is automatically controlled by machinery.

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:22.260
Though the fire is strong, but the ignition timing is rough.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:28.390
So, like the BlackBird, we'll use an ignition timing
map and let the timing be controlled by the CPU.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.690
Because the power is so strong,

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:35.220
I think the only person who can do this is Tominaga.

00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:38.740
You also like this direct feel of the carburetor, right?

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:43.570
The feel of a mechanical carburetor that you
can't get from an electronically controlled one.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:50.790
Not burning the gasoline nicely, but as though it
will break apart and explode without warning...

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:53.930
This violent and unforgiving realm,

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:57.490
we'll support it with an accurate ignition timing map.

00:06:58.340 --> 00:07:00.560
The theoretical power will not increase.

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:06.180
But that direct feel of a carburetor that you desire will be in effect.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:09.390
Sorry to have disturbed you. Do your best, Rikako-chan.

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:12.920
Eiji-san's Lan Evo will be fast.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:19.440
If you like, you can come and see me. You may get some ideas.

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:22.150
Yes, thank you, I will.

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.420
That Rikako-chan...

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.650
So, when is it going to be ready?

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:33.440
As soon as the parts are gathered.
The 4 Throttle and an imported differential.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:35.670
It should come by the end of this week.

00:07:36.280 --> 00:07:39.670
Then, including the initial setting, it'll take 10 days, right?

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:43.670
After 10 days, we'll meet at the Shibaura Parking Garage.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.470
If I'm not mistaken, it should be around here...

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:54.330
Excuse me.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:55.590
How may I help you?

00:07:55.590 --> 00:08:00.520
Do you know of a car shop, RGO Factory, around here?

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:04.170
Are you from Osaka?

00:08:08.200 --> 00:08:10.060
A guest for Eiji-san?

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:12.320
Apparently, it's his younger brother.

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:19.100
You seem to be enjoying yourself,
you must have forgotten all about Osaka.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:21.890
Maki, why did you come here? Don't tell me...

00:08:21.890 --> 00:08:23.670
Don't worry.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:28.410
I just dropped by since I brought some goods to
Ohta market on a 4-ton truck early this morning.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:31.410
I see, you're doing your best.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:36.610
Of course, it'd be a disgrace if people said our company
closed down because you're not there, wouldn't it?

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:38.350
Is Eriko-san also doing fine?

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:43.540
Yeah. I'm going back since you seem busy.

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:44.790
Wait up.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:47.500
Even if you leave know, you'll arrive
at Osaka in the middle of the night.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:49.380
If that's the case, it's the same as arriving in the morning.

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.110
Why don't you rest a while here?

00:08:51.110 --> 00:08:52.180
But...

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:55.830
This is the key to my apartment, I'll be back by 8.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:09:00.270
Until then, you can sleep a while there. The place is...

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:02.110
I'll take you there.

00:09:03.080 --> 00:09:07.100
It's my break time and I need some fresh air.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:10.280
I'll leave it to you then.

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:14.010
Later, let's eat together at the restaurant I'm working at.

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:20.070
You two don't look alike, even though you're brothers.

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:22.720
Because our parents got remarried when
both of them each had their own child.

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:24.850
Ah, I see.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:28.630
Are you my brother's girlfriend in Tokyo?

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.870
No, it's not like that.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:37.250
My brother has many girlfriends in
Osaka, too. You'd better not be serious.

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:42.320
Seems like you really like Eiji-san, right?

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:55.210
Why? Is Tokyo really that great? Isn't Osaka good enough?

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:01.520
<i>Your name is Maki, huh?</i>

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.520
<i>From today onwards, we're brothers.</i>

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.770
<i>Come one, why don't you call me "onii-chan".</i>

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:15.400
<i>I'll teach you lots of interesting things, Maki.</i>

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:20.960
Maki! Hey, Maki!

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:25.380
At least sleep on a futon. You'll catch a cold.

00:10:27.880 --> 00:10:30.330
Come on, let's go eat.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.680
Hey, hurry up!

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:39.910
Brother, does it have to be Tokyo?

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:45.210
If you want to open a car shop, you can do it in Osaka too, right?

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:50.370
Let's close down our company and open a
car shop in Osaka together! I'll also help you!

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:51.350
Maki.

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:54.100
Mother will surely agree too.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:11:00.500
Of course, I wanted to do it. I wanted to make a living with cars.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:05.110
I wanted to live my life just for cars day and night.

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:08.830
Then, let's start now, right brother?

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:14.080
I didn't choose this path because of anybody else. I chose it myself.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:16.300
Brother...

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:21.780
I'll keep my promise of three months. I will return to Osaka.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:23.840
So don't you worry, Maki.

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.820
After the BlackBird, it's this one's turn?

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:38.320
That's right, all these jobs don't pay at all.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:42.060
Good evening.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:45.800
Did you came by train?

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:48.140
Yeah, how is the Z?

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.800
It's ok. Then, let's try it out.

00:11:52.790 --> 00:11:57.940
Akio, she's the daughter of Ohta-san from RGO, Rikako-chan.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:11:59.470
Hello.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:04.150
Both of you are about the same age...

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:07.910
Don't be surprised, she's the one
assembling the engine for the Lan Evo now.

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:10.270
The Lan Evo's?

00:12:11.490 --> 00:12:14.030
Just in time, why don't you send her home?

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:29.210
<i>How unexpected, it's not a engine which can rev accurately.</i>

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:33.450
<i>I have confidence in making a smoother running engine than this.</i>

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:40.050
<i>I have it, but what is this feeling? It's not like a machine.</i>

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:44.850
<i>It's like it's alive! What's with this energetic feeling?</i>

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:50.280
Is it alright if I drop you off at RGO?

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:56.190
If it's possible, there's somewhere I'd like you to come with me.

00:13:01.790 --> 00:13:02.540
Hi!

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:10.700
It really looks fast.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:12.240
It' actually very fast,

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:13.900
its got 600hp of power,

00:13:13.900 --> 00:13:15.890
and can dish out about 80Nm2 of torque.

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:16.800
Really?!

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:21.020
Yeah, Tominaga-san said that he's
certain around that much is possible.

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:27.060
It's a strange car. I felt something within it just a glance...

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:31.020
but others can't realize its existence.

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:33.070
Only those who understand.

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:36.010
<i>I can also tell.</i>

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:41.260
<i>Whether it's Shima-san's BlackBird or this first-gen Z...</i>

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:45.530
<i>If they show me cars like these, I feel
like I can't leave Tokyo anymore...</i>

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:48.600
<i>I understand how my brother feels too.</i>

00:13:50.760 --> 00:13:53.710
Well then, brother, I'll head back.

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:56.560
If not, I'll arrive in the afternoon.

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:57.820
Ah, that's right.

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:03.390
I have one favor. Sorry to trouble you,
but would you take me back in this Z?

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:08.270
I parked my truck at Ohta market.

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:11.010
I want to sit in this car as a Tokyo souvenir.

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:13.010
Sure.

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:14.590
Maki.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:18.270
I know. I'll drive safely back to Osaka.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:22.530
And regarding our company, you don't have to worry.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.990
Surprisingly, even without you, we can handle it well.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:30.250
You should do whatever you need to do here.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:33.030
Yeah, send my regards to Mother.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.210
As expected, it's incredible!

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.960
That reminds me, you know Shima-san too, right?

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:44.290
Yes, of course.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:47.980
When he came to Osaka, he taught me a lot.

00:14:48.800 --> 00:14:53.050
His aura is like yours. My brother is also the same.

00:14:53.960 --> 00:14:55.480
I know just by sitting next to you all.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:57.170
Perhaps so.

00:14:57.170 --> 00:15:00.180
We might have the same feeling.

00:15:00.640 --> 00:15:06.560
I have friends and buddies in Osaka
but no one who can drive like this.

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.740
I, too, want to come to Tokyo.

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:21.090
Thank you. And can you tell my brother?

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:23.790
He doesn't have to return after everything is over.

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:28.700
If he really likes it here, he can stay here permanently.

00:15:28.700 --> 00:15:32.130
I roughly understand his feelings.

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:41.810
But I like Osaka. So I don't want my brother to forget about Osaka.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.000
Alright then.

00:15:54.160 --> 00:15:58.240
Oh, it's Shige's exhaust manifold. And that's the muffler?

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:00.480
Rikako?

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:05.470
Rikako, the muffler and stuff have arrived from Osaka.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.170
Seems like it's complete.

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:11.220
Yeah.

00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:14.530
The rest depends on Eiji-san's arrangement.

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:16.430
You don't look happy.

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:22.190
I feel like I've left out something.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:27.610
During assembling, everyone feels the same way.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.940
It's alright. It will be the best tuned car.

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:35.160
Here, take it.

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:41.670
This is the data during assembly, or more
like I wrote down whatever I found out.

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:48.430
I'm only in charge of the engine and you're in charge of completing it.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:52.920
Ok, just leave the rest to me. Thank you.

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:59.430
The new Porsche Turbo is, frankly speaking, too fast for the highway.

00:17:00.170 --> 00:17:04.640
Who in the world can control this 420hp machine at will?

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:09.440
I want somebody who can really control it to own it.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:16.650
I finished faster than expected.

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:24.830
<i>It's been a while since I drove at Wangan at this hour.</i>

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:30.170
<i>Nothing has changed. I'm the only one who's changed.</i>

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:34.810
<i>That car is fast, is it a GT-R?</i>

00:17:35.930 --> 00:17:38.550
<i>No, it's not an R.</i>

00:17:39.630 --> 00:17:40.630
<i>Z?</i>

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:42.940
<i>I was driving at 180km/h according to the meter,</i>

00:17:42.940 --> 00:17:45.900
<i>and it was still accelerating, I couldn't catch up at all.</i>

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.560
<i>I'll never be beaten by a normal Z.</i>

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:55.540
<i>But if that's the car they call the Devil Z...</i>

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:57.830
<i>It can't be... that Z?!</i>

00:18:07.420 --> 00:18:09.310
<i>So that's the Devil Z...</i>

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:19.010
I heard they're going out again tonight.

00:18:20.380 --> 00:18:23.370
Yesterday too, they were doing warm ups on the car all night.

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:25.690
I think she made a good engine.

00:18:26.740 --> 00:18:28.890
You wanted a son like that, right?

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:33.240
I won't deny that...

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:37.870
If Rikako wants to take over RGO, I'll let her do it.

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:42.060
Being male or female doesn't matter, however she has good skills.

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:43.250
You're right.

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:46.120
However, she cannot do it alone.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:54.210
The reason RGO could survive until today,
is because you stayed by my side.

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:57.020
What's gotten onto you...

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:04.550
It's been already three months...
does Eiji really intend to return to Osaka?

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:08.780
Ok.

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:10.190
It's time, right?

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:18.270
Great, I made it in time!

00:19:19.240 --> 00:19:20.610
Made it in time... for?

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:22.990
The filming location was prolonged.

00:19:23.780 --> 00:19:25.490
You'll give me a ride, right?

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:27.800
Again?

00:19:27.800 --> 00:19:31.360
If you do, I'll give you another piece of valuable information.

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:34.880
I heard that the Lan Evo's setting has been completed.

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:37.090
Is this also from boss Yamamoto?

00:19:37.090 --> 00:19:42.800
Yeah, it seems that he'll race with BlackBird tonight.

00:19:43.550 --> 00:19:47.820
Why is it in such good condition? It's still only 5500rpm.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:51.480
If you rev until the limit of 8000rpm, you'll faint!

00:19:51.480 --> 00:19:55.190
Seriously I might. It really is great.

00:19:55.190 --> 00:20:00.030
How can a 4G63 engine of a Lan Evo feel so good?

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:06.290
Say, Eiji-san, are you really going to return to Osaka?

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:09.500
Tokyo is different from Osaka...

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:12.550
even though, it's like Osaka, full of buildings,

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:16.170
and overflowing with people and cars.

00:20:17.220 --> 00:20:19.760
But it's not that I dislike it, I like it.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:24.060
Frankly, I never thought I'd fit in Tokyo's lifestyle so well.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:31.330
If you stay here forever, if you desire it Eiji-san, you can do it easily.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.370
Tokyo will become your town.

00:20:34.570 --> 00:20:39.130
Tokyo is fun, everyday is like a dream.

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:42.070
Frankly, I want to stay in this town forever.

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:43.980
Why not do so then?

00:20:43.980 --> 00:20:45.010
But I will go back,

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:49.040
to settle my feelings once and for all.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.540
I'm a person from Osaka.

00:20:52.540 --> 00:20:56.040
I have people waiting for me in Osaka.

00:20:56.040 --> 00:21:01.540
Well, let's rev until the limit, complete its
warm-up for our most powerful opponent.

00:21:03.510 --> 00:21:06.170
It seems pretty fast now after completion.

00:21:06.170 --> 00:21:08.890
I think it's actually really fast.

00:21:09.490 --> 00:21:11.660
Meaning it's in its ultimate form?

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:12.640
Exactly!

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:18.250
Then the course is... for the time being, 2-3 rounds
around C1's outer-course, then into Wangan.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.380
Understood.

00:21:19.380 --> 00:21:22.650
For a while, can you drive ahead of us?

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.960
You intend to check them out throughly, right?

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:27.910
That's right.

00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:33.420
I want to see what the rumored BlackBird
is made of, properly from behind.

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:39.520
Fine with me. From the movement
of the car until the way it's driven...

00:21:39.520 --> 00:21:42.480
please observe everything one by one, from the eyes of a builder.

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:48.050
If we aren't careful, he'll pull away in a flash.

00:21:48.050 --> 00:21:51.050
It's alright, he's still not going all out.

00:21:51.050 --> 00:21:55.150
Perhaps he's concerned that we still need to warm up.

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:00.750
Even at this time, you're resetting?

00:22:01.510 --> 00:22:03.900
For the time being, I'm just observing the monitor.

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:07.060
Fast!

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:09.310
Isn't it over-revving?

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:12.160
So far so good, it's maintaining 6500rpm.

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:14.660
That car, it's too amazing!

00:22:27.300 --> 00:22:30.120
It feels different from the last time we drove,

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:32.060
did you do something to the differential?

00:22:32.060 --> 00:22:33.360
Oh, you're pretty sharp.

00:22:34.210 --> 00:22:38.370
When I was installing the imported final gear,
I changed the torque distribution.

00:22:38.370 --> 00:22:44.560
Originally, it's 50-50, but I fixed it to 35 in front and 65 at the back.

00:22:44.560 --> 00:22:47.310
So, how is it? Is it faster?

00:22:47.310 --> 00:22:51.830
I wonder. But the handling has improved, no doubt about it.

00:22:55.050 --> 00:22:56.750
We're entering Wangan.

00:22:56.750 --> 00:23:00.910
Shifting to high gear using the imported
final gear, revving up to the 8000rpm limit.

00:23:00.910 --> 00:23:05.680
Ok. Time for the final warm-up.
Let's see if this is the real thing or not.

00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:07.690
At last, they're starting to get serious.

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:19.280
Here comes the Z. Now all the players are gathered!
